    "body": "#### vim-patch:9.2.1253: filetype: NLP files are not recognized\r\n\r\nProblem:  filetype: NLP files are not recognized\r\nSolution: Detect *.nlp files as nlp filetype\r\n          (David de Hilster)\r\n\r\nReference:\r\nhttps://visualtext.org/nlp/\r\nhttps://github.com/VisualText/nlp-engine\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21480\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/62cbfe998552aed8ee54833ba4df9e42606530c6\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: David de Hilster <dehilster@gmail.com>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:fd0253d: runtime(cpp): syntax highlighting can be improved\r\n\r\nThis is a combination of the following changes:\r\n\r\nProblem:  The C++11 raw strings pattern is slow because its leading\r\n          lookbehind prevents an efficient search.\r\nSolution: Force the backtracking engine for the attribute start pattern.\r\n\r\nProblem:  The C++ attribute start pattern is slow because its leading lookbehind\r\n          prevents an efficient search.\r\nSolution: Force the backtracking engine for the attribute start pattern.\r\n\r\nProblem:  The slice bracket highlighting incurs avoidable cost on large buffers.\r\nSolution: Split the rule into separate literal matches for `[:` and `:]`,\r\n\r\nProblem:  The GNU C++ min/max operator rule incurs avoidable cost on large\r\n          buffers.\r\nSolution: Split the rule into separate literal matches for `<?` and `>?`,\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21513\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/fd0253d46825b358ee3a99081d933644684309f1\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Julien Voisin <julien.voisin@dustri.org>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:9.2.1254: filetype: Bats files are detected as sh\r\n\r\nProblem:  Bats test files are detected as \"sh\", so plugins and parsers\r\n          cannot tell them apart from plain Bash scripts, and Bats\r\n          extensions are highlighted as plain Bash: the \"test\" in \"@test\"\r\n          is highlighted as the test command and the test body is not a\r\n          function body, so it does not fold.\r\nSolution: Detect *.bats files and bats shebang lines as \"bats\", include\r\n          filetype, indent and syntax scripts that reuse the \"sh\" ones\r\n          with b:is_bash set, highlight @test with its name and fold its\r\n          body like a function, highlight \"# bats test_tags=\" and\r\n          \"file_tags=\" comments and the commands bats-core provides, and\r\n          add a syntax test (Grant Hutchins).\r\n\r\nBats (Bash Automated Testing System) test files are Bash with extensions\r\nsuch as `@test \"name\" { ... }` blocks, which Bash parsers like\r\ntree-sitter-bash do not understand.  Tools that do need a filetype to key\r\non: bash-language-server parses .bats files with a bats dialect, ALE has\r\nbats linters, and tree-sitter-bats provides a grammar for editors that\r\nuse tree-sitter.  Highlighting, indenting and the \"sh\" filetype plugin\r\nbehave as before, the same way the \"bash\" filetype works.\r\n\r\nCommands from add-on libraries such as bats-assert are not highlighted.\r\n\r\nrelated: vim/vim#14039\r\ncloses:  vim/vim#21516\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/d8ae4348a0393c7e2b03f68541c3d1d920292165\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Grant Hutchins <git@nertzy.com>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:c1f545e: runtime(yaml): syntax highlighting can be improved\r\n\r\nThis is a combination of the following changes:\r\n\r\nProblem:  PyYAML timestamp matching scans positions that cannot begin a\r\n          timestamp.\r\nSolution: Check for a leading digit before timestamp boundary matching.\r\n\r\nProblem:  The PyYAML integer and floats pattern repeats the optional\r\n          sign in each alternative.\r\nSolution: Match the optional sign once before the alternatives.\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21521\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/c1f545e7aad552e99383e458b11e64d7b3a419fa\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Julien Voisin <julien.voisin@dustri.org>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:44a80f9: runtime(tasm): Update syntax, add missing condition codes\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21532\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/44a80f9449f1c81c8cad153167d637c6809143ec\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: Brad Forschinger <github@bnjf.id.au>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:89c8c0a: runtime(debchangelog): Update runtime file\r\n\r\nThis is a combination of the following changes:\r\n\r\n- debchangelog: Handle newer \" b1 - \" prefixed apt-listbugs output\r\n- debchangelog: Use only command name, not full path, to apt-listbugs\r\n- debchangelog: Escape g:debchangelog_listbugs_severities argument to apt-listbugs\r\n\r\nrelated: vim/vim#21559\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/89c8c0a680b333de8504bf7f05ec8a6635936d6d\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: James McCoy <jamessan@debian.org>\r\n\r\n\r\n#### vim-patch:5287a96: runtime(debversions): Update runtime file\r\n\r\nThis is a combination of the following changes:\r\n- debversions: Move questing to unsupported\r\n- debversions: Add Tenacious T-Rex (27.04)\r\n- debversions: Move bookworm to unsupported\r\n- debversions: Query for each executable once\r\n- debversions: try getting data from distro-info\r\n\r\ncloses: vim/vim#21559\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/vim/vim/commit/5287a96500f94faeb2daf7ae2108e28090d269ca\r\n\r\nCo-authored-by: James McCoy <jamessan@debian.org>",
